        <!-- Legend -->
        <mxCell id="legend" value="LEGEND&#10;&#10;&#9644; Blue  = agent workflow (claude -p, tier-agnostic; never runs git, never names a model)&#10;&#9670; Orange = khazad-dum gate / decision (runs the project&#39;s test_commands — the REAL result, not the agent&#39;s self-report)&#10;&#9679; Green  = start / success terminal      &#9679; Red = human escalation      &#9633; Purple note = special handling&#10;&#10;TDD beat = Red &#8594; Green &#8594; Refactor. Both refactor workflows (2.1.8 enabling, 2.1.9 cleanup) are BEHAVIOUR-PRESERVING:&#10;they change structure, never what a test asserts. A slice that must CHANGE existing behaviour is routed to a human (not automated).&#10;Refactor failure asymmetry: enabling-refactor (2.1.8) fail &#8594; human (blocks); cleanup-refactor (2.1.9) fail &#8594; revert to green commit &amp; proceed (non-blocking).&#10;&#10;khazad-dum owns ALL version control: checks out feature branch, commits at each passed gate, pushes / opens the PR at the end.&#10;Escalation ladder (every build/test gate): retry at same tier within a per-tier budget, then climb haiku/medium &#8594; sonnet/medium &#8594; opus/high &#8594; human.&#10;All thresholds / budgets / loop-guards / refactor enable-flags live in .khazad-dum/config.json. Each workflow writes one report to .khazad-dum/orchestration_log/&lt;feature&gt;/." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="200" y="2460" width="1300" height="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

